# Shell scripts must check out with LF on every platform.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text
# files to CRLF in the working copy. A CRLF `#!/usr/bin/env bash` line makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter named "bash\r", and the release runner fails with
# `bad interpreter` naming env, which exists, rather than the carriage return,
# which is the problem.
*.sh text eol=lf
